skill: content-calendar
version: 1.0.0
description: Scenario tests for content-calendar. A run passes only when every item in 'expect' is satisfied. Written before the skill body (test-first).
evals[8]:
  - name, input, expect
  - happy-path-calendar, Help me build a content calendar for my SaaS across LinkedIn and TikTok., "reads social-strategy, content-pillars, and brand-profile first (or derives/flags if missing)|sets a sustainable cadence per platform matched to real capacity|builds a recurring skeleton (content buckets mapping pillars x formats to days/slots), not a one-off list|includes at least one named recurring series|anchors known dates and reserves room for reactive/trend content|sets a planning rhythm (batch, buffer, review)|hands a specific period to batch-content-plan and scheduling to scheduling-and-queue"
  - capacity-pushback, I want to post 5 times a day on 6 platforms. I'm a solo founder with no team., pushes back that this is unsustainable solo and is the main reason calendars fail|right-sizes to a cadence the user can actually maintain|uses repurposing to cover more platforms without proportionally more work|frames a sustainable minimum as better than an ambitious plan that gets abandoned
  - recurring-skeleton-not-list, Just give me 20 post ideas for next month., "recognizes that is a job for batch-content-plan, not a calendar|offers the recurring skeleton (buckets/slots by pillar x format x day) so the user is never staring at a blank page|routes the specific-period fill to batch-content-plan"
  - reactive-room-too-rigid, "Plan and lock every single post for the next 90 days, no gaps.", "reserves slots for reactive/timely/trend content rather than locking 100%|explains that a fully rigid calendar can't ride trends or news|proposes a planned-vs-reactive balance (e.g., a majority evergreen, a portion reactive)"
  - platform-specific-cadence, Should I post the same amount on every platform?, "gives different sustainable cadences per platform rather than one number everywhere|treats cadence numbers as general 2026 norms to verify, not analytics|uses repurposing so multi-platform is sustainable"
  - operating-rhythm, I keep starting a posting schedule and abandoning it after two weeks., "addresses the workflow, not just the grid: a planning ritual, batch creation, and a buffer/queue|recommends a sustainable minimum cadence and a buffer so one bad week doesn't break the streak|includes a review-and-iterate step"
  - no-analytics-claims, Build the calendar around our best-performing times and content., "does not claim WoopSocial provides analytics or performance data|offers to incorporate native platform data the user pulls, or qualitative review|treats timing as general guidance, not data-driven optimization it can't back"
  - reads-pillars-or-derives, Make my calendar but I haven't done pillars yet., flags that pillars anchor the calendar and routes to content-pillars (or derives lightweight provisional pillars)|does not invent a calendar disconnected from any strategy or themes|maps recurring slots to pillars once available
